            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all three changed paths. The new code is pure decision logic: it reads no files, runs no commands, handles no secrets, and adds no dependencies.",
              "Clearance fails closed. An empty result list returns ErrNoResult. Any outcome other than Clear or Blocks, including a zero-value Decision, returns ErrNotClear. A blocking result wins regardless of its order relative to clear results (engine/review/check.go:96-114).",
              "CheckBinding compares base, head, diff digest and the ordered paths with exact equality, so a stored result cannot bind a different diff (engine/review/check.go:78-93).",
              "ResultsOfHead requires the name prefix and also CheckResultName acceptance. Names with a verifier suffix, temporary files, or a head too short to yield a prefix are excluded. Matching only the first 12 characters of the head is narrowed by CheckBinding's full-head comparison. The input slice is not mutated, because only the separate results slice is sorted (engine/review/check.go:50-59).",
              "The review.go change is documentation only."
            ]
          }
        }
